WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.320
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:07.339
Walmart is the largest company in the world,
and the biggest employer in the U.S. pulling

00:00:07.339 --> 00:00:11.969
in $469 billion in revenue every year.

00:00:11.969 --> 00:00:17.880
Out of the top 7 revenue generating companies
in the world, Walmart is the only one that

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.510
doesn't deal in oil and gas.

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:27.580
In fact every year, everyone in the world
will make an average of 1.1 purchases at a

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:31.240
Walmart store.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:38.220
Walmart has 2.1 million full-time employees.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:41.350
That's seven times the population of Iceland.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:49.660
In 2012, Walmart registered approximately
$444 billion in sales, which is $20 billion

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:52.559
more than Austria's GDP.

00:00:52.559 --> 00:00:58.609
If Walmart were a country, it would be the
26th largest economy in the world

00:00:58.609 --> 00:01:03.840
If Walmart was an army, it would have the
second largest military in the world, behind

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.440
China.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:11.890
Walmart is bigger than Home Depot, Target,
Sears, and Costco combined.

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:16.430
In 2009, Walmart sold more bananas than any
other item.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:22.680
If Walmart's more than 900 million square
feet of retail space were spread out over

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:31.410
one place it would take up roughly 34 miles,
which is about 1.5 times the size of Manhattan.

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:37.320
Walmart parking lots alone take up roughly
the size of Tampa, Florida.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:45.170
In 2000, Walmart was sued 4,851 times, or
about once every 2 hours.

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:50.240
90 percent of all Americans live within 15
miles of a Walmart.

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:56.200
The most frequent destination typed into Telenav
GPS devices is Walmart.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:04.810
Roughly 4,700 (about 90 percent) of international
stores operate under a banner other than Walmart,

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:14.040
including Asda in the UK, Seiyu in Japan,
and Best Price in India.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:22.599
An additional Walmart Supercenter per 100,000
residents increases average BMI by 0.25 units

00:02:22.599 --> 00:02:26.340
and the obesity rate by 2.4 percent.

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:31.189
8 cents for every U.S. dollar is spent at
Walmart.

00:02:31.189 --> 00:02:38.209
On average, about 100 stores go out of business
in the area surrounding a town with a new

00:02:38.209 --> 00:02:39.389
Walmart store.

00:02:39.389 --> 00:02:44.519
Walmart's CEO Mike Duke makes sure to keep
his employees paid, but that doesn't mean

00:02:44.519 --> 00:02:46.879
he doesn't keep some for himself.

00:02:46.879 --> 00:02:54.400
In 2010, his $35 million salary caused him
to earn more in just one hour than the average

00:02:54.400 --> 00:03:00.720
Walmart employee makes in a full year!

